# Prisma Rules

Policy: [docs/DATABASE.md](docs/DATABASE.md), backup: [docs/ops/BACKUP.md](docs/ops/BACKUP.md)

- Source of truth is `prisma/schema.prisma` only — never introduce schema drift outside Prisma.
- Every schema change needs a migration plus rollback / risk notes.
- Before production `prisma migrate deploy`, require a DB backup (see BACKUP.md).
- Respect existing conventions: UUID PKs, tenant via `company` / `branch`, soft delete fields as defined per model.
- Prefer Prisma enums for important statuses/types; avoid ad-hoc string columns when an enum already fits.
- Split ORM/schema upgrades from framework/runtime upgrades when possible.

# Verification

- `npx prisma generate` succeeds after schema edits.
- Migration applies cleanly in the intended environment (`migrate dev` local / `migrate deploy` staging-prod).
- Record known caveats or temporary exceptions in DATABASE.md or db-blueprint — do not leave silent drift.
